<%
  # Never output a raw @mention or issue reference: usernames, and any other text containing
  # "@" or "#", go in code spans so nobody gets pinged and no issue gets a back-reference.
  # Text is kept on one line (a line break would end the code span and the table row),
  # and pipes are escaped so they don't break the table.
  safe = lambda do |text|
    text = text.to_s.tr("`", "'").gsub(/[[:space:]]+/, " ").strip.gsub("|", "\\|")
    text.match?(/[@#]/) ? "`#{text}`" : text
  end
  login = lambda { |name| "`@#{name.to_s.gsub(/[`[:space:]]/, "")}`" }
  github_label = lambda do |person|
    person[:name].to_s.empty? ? login.call(person[:login]) : "#{login.call(person[:login])} (#{safe.call(person[:name])})"
  end
  zenodo_cell = lambda do |match|
    if match.nil?
      "❌ Not found"
    elsif match[:orcids]
      "⚠️ Different ORCID: #{safe.call(match[:person][:name])} has #{safe.call(match[:orcids][1])} (paper: #{safe.call(match[:orcids][0])})"
    elsif match[:status] == :exact
      "✅ #{safe.call(match[:person][:name])}"
    else
      "⚠️ Written differently: #{safe.call(match[:person][:name])}"
    end
  end
  github_cell = lambda do |match|
    if match.nil?
      "❌ Not found"
    elsif match[:status] == :close
      "⚠️ Possibly #{github_label.call(match[:person])}"
    else
      "✅ #{github_label.call(match[:person])}"
    end
  end
  zenodo_checked = !report[:zenodo_only].nil?
  github_checked = !report[:github_only].nil?
-%>
**Authors check**

| Paper author | Zenodo archive | GitHub contributor |
|---|---|---|
<% report[:authors].each do |row| -%>
| <%= safe.call(row[:author][:name]) %> | <%= zenodo_checked ? zenodo_cell.call(row[:zenodo]) : "—" %> | <%= github_checked ? github_cell.call(row[:github]) : "—" %> |
<% end -%>
<% if zenodo_checked && report[:zenodo_only].any? -%>

**Zenodo authors not listed in the paper:**
<% report[:zenodo_only].each do |creator| -%>
- <%= safe.call(creator[:name]) %>
<% end -%>
<% end -%>
<% if github_checked && report[:github_only].any? -%>

**GitHub contributors not matched to a paper author** (reviewers, editor and bots excluded):
<% report[:github_only].each do |contributor| -%>
- <%= github_label.call(contributor) %>: <%= contributor[:contributions] %> commit<%= contributor[:contributions] == 1 ? "" : "s" %>
<% end -%>
<% end -%>
<% notes.each do |note| -%>

_<%= note %>_
<% end -%>

<details>
<summary>How to read this</summary>

- ✅ The name matches. For Zenodo, "Last, First" and "First Last" count as the same.
- ⚠️ Zenodo: the name is written differently (accents, capitalization, initials, typos), or the paper and Zenodo have different ORCIDs. GitHub: probably the same person, but the editor should confirm.
- ❌ No match found.

GitHub only lists people who made commits, so authors who contributed in other ways won't appear there. Contributors don't all need to be authors. These results are for the editor to review, not a pass/fail check.
</details>
